---
import '../styles/hyrox-theme.css';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>subninety.club — What HYROX racing actually looks like</title>
<meta name="description" content="Race reports and analysis of HYROX racing built from real athlete data — heart rate, calorie burn, cadence, recovery. Every chart is one athlete's hardware in one race; every conclusion has its data.">

<!-- Open Graph / Social Media -->
<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
<meta property="og:site_name" content="subninety.club" />
<meta property="og:url" content="https://subninety.club/" />
<meta property="og:title" content="subninety.club — What HYROX racing actually looks like" />
<meta property="og:description" content="Race reports and analysis of HYROX racing built from real athlete data — heart rate, calorie burn, cadence, recovery." />
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
<meta name="twitter:title" content="subninety.club — What HYROX racing actually looks like" />
<meta name="twitter:description" content="Race reports and analysis of HYROX racing built from real athlete data." />

<link rel="canonical" href="https://subninety.club/" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght,SOFT,WONK@9..144,400;9..144,500;9..144,700;9..144,900&family=Inter+Tight:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  "name": "subninety.club",
  "url": "https://subninety.club/",
  "description": "Race reports and analysis of HYROX racing built from real athlete data.",
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Prashant Singh"
  }
}
</script>

<style>
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink-1); }
body {
  font-family: 'Inter Tight', system-ui, sans-serif;
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.65;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  font-feature-settings: "ss01" on, "cv11" on;
}
a { color: inherit; }

.wrap { max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 80px 24px 96px; }

.mission { margin-bottom: 96px; max-width: 880px; }
.mission-text {
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: clamp(40px, 5.6vw, 68px);
  line-height: 1.02;
  letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  margin: 0 0 28px;
  color: var(--ink-1);
  font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 50;
}
.mission-text em {
  font-style: italic;
  color: var(--yellow);
  font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 100;
}
.mission-sub {
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-size: clamp(20px, 1.7vw, 24px);
  line-height: 1.45;
  color: var(--ink-2);
  margin: 0 0 36px;
  font-variation-settings: "SOFT" 100, "opsz" 32;
}
.author-intro {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 12px;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  padding-top: 24px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
}
.author-intro strong { color: var(--ink-1); font-weight: 500; }

.featured { margin-bottom: 64px; }
.featured-eyebrow {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  margin-bottom: 16px;
}
.featured-card {
  display: block;
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding: 48px;
  text-decoration: none;
  color: inherit;
  transition: border-color 0.2s, background 0.2s;
}
.featured-card:hover { border-color: var(--yellow); background: #181820; }
.featured-card h2 {
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
  line-height: 1.1;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  margin: 0 0 20px;
  color: var(--ink-1);
}
.featured-card .featured-desc {
  color: var(--ink-2);
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.6;
  margin-bottom: 32px;
  max-width: 720px;
}
.featured-meta {
  display: flex;
  gap: 32px;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  padding-top: 24px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
}
.featured-meta .stat strong {
  display: block;
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-size: 22px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  color: var(--ink-1);
  text-transform: none;
  margin-bottom: 4px;
}

/* Key Takeaways */
.takeaways-homepage {
  background: var(--surface);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding: 36px 40px;
  margin-bottom: 96px;
}
.takeaways-homepage h2.takeaways-h {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--yellow);
  font-weight: 500;
  margin: 0 0 24px;
}
.takeaways-homepage ol {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(360px, 1fr));
  gap: 8px;
}
.takeaways-homepage li {
  padding: 18px 24px 18px 20px;
  border-left: 2px solid var(--yellow);
  font-size: 15.5px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  color: var(--ink-1);
}
.takeaways-homepage li .n {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  color: var(--yellow);
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
  font-weight: 500;
}
.takeaways-homepage li strong { color: var(--ink-1); font-weight: 600; }
.takeaways-homepage li a {
  color: var(--yellow);
  text-decoration: none;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 230, 0, 0.3);
}

.section-head {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  margin-bottom: 28px;
  padding-top: 16px;
}
.analysis { margin-bottom: 96px; }
.analysis-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
  gap: 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
}
.analysis-item {
  display: block;
  padding: 28px 32px 28px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  text-decoration: none;
  color: inherit;
  transition: padding-left 0.2s, background 0.2s;
}
.analysis-item:hover { padding-left: 16px; background: var(--surface); }
.analysis-item h3 {
  font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: 20px;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  margin: 0 0 8px;
  color: var(--ink-1);
}
.analysis-item p { margin: 0; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-2); }

.coming { margin-bottom: 64px; }
.coming-list {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--ink-2);
  line-height: 2.2;
}
.coming-list li::before { content: "→ "; color: var(--ink-3); }

.site-footer {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding-top: 36px;
  margin-top: 96px;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: var(--ink-3);
  line-height: 1.7;
}

@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .wrap { padding: 48px 18px 64px; }
  .featured-card { padding: 28px 24px; }
  .takeaways-homepage { padding: 24px 22px; }
  .analysis-item { padding: 22px 0; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/">subninety<span class="dot">.</span>club</a>
    <nav class="site-nav">
      <a href="/hyrox-bengaluru-2026/">Race reports</a>
      <a href="/hyrox-calories-burned/">Analysis</a>
      <a href="/about/">About</a>
      <a href="/method/">Method</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <section class="mission">
    <h1 class="mission-text">
      What HYROX racing actually looks like, from <em>one athlete's data</em>.
    </h1>
    <p class="mission-sub">
      Race reports and analysis built from heart rate, calorie burn, cadence, and recovery
      data captured during real HYROX races. Every chart cites its source. Every conclusion
      shows its data.
    </p>
    <div class="author-intro">
      By <strong>Prashant Singh</strong> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Age group 30&ndash;34 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
      Bengaluru &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Race time <strong>02:01:06</strong>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="featured">
    <div class="featured-eyebrow">Featured race report</div>
    <a class="featured-card" href="/hyrox-bengaluru-2026/">
      <h2>What heart rate looks like during a HYROX race &mdash; Bengaluru 2026</h2>
      <p class="featured-desc">
        1,157 heart rate samples from a 2:01:06 finish, broken down by all 16 segments.
        92% of the race spent at threshold or above. Five charts covering zone distribution,
        per-segment effort, drift, and post-station recovery &mdash; built from one
        athlete&rsquo;s Apple Watch hardware and the official HYROX timing system.
      </p>
      <div class="featured-meta">
        <div class="stat"><strong>1,157</strong>HR samples</div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>189 bpm</strong>peak</div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>92%</strong>at threshold+</div>
        <div class="stat"><strong>5</strong>charts, 1 race</div>
      </div>
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="takeaways-homepage">
    <h2 class="takeaways-h">Key takeaways</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <span class="n">01 &mdash; What this is</span>
        <strong>A single-athlete HYROX research archive.</strong> One person&rsquo;s body,
        one race so far, eleven charts. Built from primary data, not aggregated content.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">02 &mdash; What the data says</span>
        <strong>HYROX is functionally a 2-hour threshold race.</strong> 92% of a 2:01:06
        finish was spent at threshold or above &mdash; not an interval workout with rest breaks.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">03 &mdash; Methodology</span>
        <strong>Every number is traceable.</strong> Sources, sampling rates, accuracy caveats,
        and the full data pipeline are documented at <a href="/method/">/method/</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="n">04 &mdash; Cadence</span>
        <strong>New analysis weekly.</strong> Five more pieces in production from the same
        race data: cadence, recovery curves, pacing, time allocation, and timing accuracy.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="analysis">
    <div class="section-head">Analysis from this race</div>
    <div class="analysis-grid">
      <a class="analysis-item" href="/hyrox-calories-burned/">
        <h3>How many calories does HYROX burn?</h3>
        <p>1,441 kcal across the race, broken down station by station. Wall Balls and Sled Pull tied as the costliest segments.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="coming">
    <div class="section-head">In production</div>
    <ul class="coming-list">
      <li>Heart rate and cadence overlay &mdash; how your body keeps tempo through HYROX</li>
      <li>Recovery curves &mdash; what happens to HR in the 90 seconds after each station</li>
      <li>Running pace decay &mdash; how each of the 8 runs compares to the first</li>
      <li>Where the time goes &mdash; running vs stations vs roxzone, visualised</li>
      <li>Cadence-validated timing &mdash; what the watch saw vs what the chip mat saw</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    subninety.club &copy; 2026 Prashant Singh.<br />
    Built on Astro &middot; Hosted on Cloudflare Pages &middot; Data from Apple Watch Series 9 and HYROX official results.
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>